From: Custom TLS Fingerprint <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] content/devtools: add Emulation.setTLSFingerprint CDP command

Extends the DevTools Emulation domain with two new commands:
  Emulation.setTLSFingerprint  — activate custom TLS ClientHello params
  Emulation.resetTLSFingerprint — revert to Chromium defaults

The handler converts CDP parameters (or a JA3 string) to a direct call on
NetworkService via GetNetworkService(), which propagates to the network
service process through the SetTLSFingerprint Mojo method added in patch 3.

